[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605110227-gpu-cross-provider-pricing-research", :adr/title "GPU cross-provider pricing research (Vultr / RunPod / DigitalOcean) — 2026-05-11", :adr/status "active", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR 2605110227 — GPU cross-provider pricing research\n\nResearch input — does not supersede an existing ADR. Feeds:\n- **2605110100** (A40 1/3 × 2 node consolidation, blocked on UKO-46CXG)\n- **2605092000–2605092300** (Bonsai cultivar / FP8 colocation / continuous metabolic training)\n- **2605010000** (RunPod 6000 Ada unified pod)\n\nOperating Entity: etzhayyim. Vendor: etzhayyim Japan株式会社.\n\n## 0. Source data persistence\n\n| Layer | Status | Location |\n|---|---|---|\n| Raw price points (15 GPU models, 32 plans, 32 edges, MV, 3 IDX) | ✅ persisted | RW `dev.public.vertex_research_gpu_model` / `vertex_research_gpu_plan` / `edge_research_plan_uses_gpu` / `mv_research_gpu_price_compare` |\n| v3 INSERTs (DO 8× bundles + 12-mo reserved + MI350X + B300; +2 models, +8 plans, +8 edges) | ❌ sneak-dropped under barrier latency | retry pending RW quiescence |\n| v2 schema additions (`vertex_research_gpu_provider` + `edge_research_provider_offers_plan` + 7 provider rows) | ❌ DDL stuck at 0% then CANCEL'd | retry pending RW quiescence |\n| Analysis markdown | ✅ | `_working/keiei/gpu-pricing-analysis-2026-05-11.md` + `gpu-price-research-2026-05-11.sql` (v1) + `…-v2.sql` + `…-v3-data-only.sql` |\n\nSchema-convention note: existing tables landed in `public.*` not `graphar.*` because RW\n`dev` database has no `graphar` schema (only `yata_*`, `public`, `sqlmesh`). CLAUDE.md\n`graphar.*` references are aspirational; reconcile is a separate task tracked outside\nthis ADR.\n\n## 1. Headline findings\n\n### 1.1 Single-GPU $/hr (apples-to-apples overlap)\n\n| GPU | VRAM | Vultr Cloud | Vultr BM | RunPod Secure | DO On-demand | DO Reserved (12mo) | Cheapest |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A40 | 48 | $1.71 | — | **$0.44** | — | — | RunPod (3.92× cheaper than Vultr) |\n| L40 (no S) | 48 | — | $2.06 | **$0.99** | — | — | RunPod |\n| L40S | 48 | $1.54 | — | **$0.79** | $1.57 | — | RunPod (Vultr ≈ DO Bandwidth Alliance prem.) |\n| RTX 6000 Ada | 48 | — | — | **$0.74** | $1.57 | — | RunPod |\n| RTX 4000 Ada | 20 | — | — | — | $0.76 | — | DO only |\n| A100 80GB | 80 | — | $2.40–2.58 | **$1.64–1.74** | — | — | RunPod |\n| H100 SXM | 80 | — | $2.75 | $2.99 | $3.39 | **$2.50** | DO Reserved |\n| H100 PCIe | 80 | — | — | **$2.39** | — | — | RunPod only |\n| H200 | 141 | — | — | $3.59 | **$3.44** | — | DO |\n| GH200 | 96 | — | **$2.75** | — | — | — | Vultr only |\n| MI300X | 192 | — | $3.67 | $2.49 | $1.99 | **$1.88** | DO Reserved (49% cheaper than Vultr) |\n| MI325X | 256 | — | $4.25 | — | — | **$2.10** | DO Reserved (51% cheaper than Vultr) |\n| MI355X | 288 | — | **$2.59** | — | — | — | Vultr only (CDNA4 cheapest) |\n| MI350X | 288 | — | — | — | — | $3.18 | DO only |\n| B200 | 180 | — | $7.83 | $5.99 | — | — | RunPod |\n| B300 | 288 | — | — | — | — | $5.65 | DO only (Blackwell next-gen) |\n| A16 | 64 | $1.88 | — | — | — | — | Vultr only |\n\n### 1.2 Provider capability matrix\n\n| Provider | B2 free egress | K8s native | Managed K8s | SOC2 | Billing | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Vultr Cloud GPU | ✓ | ✓ | VKE | ✓ | per-hour | A40/A16/L40S only at LAX-limited inventory |\n| Vultr Bare Metal | ✓ | self-managed | — | ✓ | monthly | A100 / H100 SXM / L40 / GH200 / MI300X / MI325X / MI355X / B200 |\n| DigitalOcean | ✓ | ✓ | DOKS | ✓ | per-hour | H100 / H200 / MI300X / MI325X / MI350X / B300 reserved + Ada family on-demand |\n| RunPod Secure | ✗ | ✗ (Slurm-only Instant Cluster) | — | ✓ (Type II) | per-second | full lineup except A16, MI325X+ |\n| Equinix Metal | ✓ | self-managed | — | ✓ | monthly | quote-only, enterprise procurement |\n| Cloudflare Workers AI | ✓ | N/A (serverless fn) | — | ✓ | per-token | only for hosted models |\n\n### 1.3 Pattern\n\n- **Prosumer Ada (L40S, 6000 Ada, A40)** → RunPod halves Vultr/DO. Bandwidth-Alliance premium is real on these SKUs.\n- **Enterprise Hopper / CDNA3 (H100, H200, MI300X)** → DO Reserved is 9–49% under Vultr BM. AMD gap is the largest.\n- **Blackwell / CDNA4 (B200/B300, MI350X, MI355X)** → fragmented. Vultr MI355X $2.59/GPU/hr is the cheapest CDNA4. DO B300 reserved $5.65 is the only B-class > B200 path.\n- **Ampere legacy (A40, A100)** → DO retired. Vultr A100 ($2.58 8×) and RunPod A40 ($0.44) split the market.\n- **NVIDIA legacy (L40 no-S, GH200)** → Vultr only.\n\n## 2. Decision implications\n\n### 2.1 Kotoba/Datomic node pool (current pain point: compute-1 over-limit on `vhf-16c-58gb × 2`)\n\n| Option | $/mo | Compute fit | Notes |\n|---|---:|---|---|\n| **Hold current `vhf-16c-58gb × 2`** | $640 | tight (compute-1 24Gi vs 28Gi req, eviction tier ⚠) | needs limit reconcile (helm vs scaling-contract drift, 24Gi live vs 15Gi recovery profile) |\n| Vultr A40 1/3 × 2 (2605110100) | ~$890 (with B2 + storage) | adds GPU for ComfyUI + keiei-llm | **blocked on UKO-46CXG** |\n| **DO `gpu-mi300x-1` × 2** | ~$2,900 (24×7) | over-spec, 192GB VRAM each | viable for cohort training; massive over-spec for RW alone |\n| **DO `gpu-l40s-1` × 2** | ~$2,290 | 48GB VRAM each | mid-option |\n| Stay on `vhf-16c-58gb × 2` + RunPod for GPU | $640 + per-second | RW separated, GPU bursty | most flexible if no Vultr VKE GPU unlock |\n\n**Recommendation**: keep Kotoba/Datomic on non-GPU VKE pool until UKO-46CXG resolves. Do not migrate RW onto DO/Vultr GPU just to colocate; the savings don't justify the topology churn.\n\n### 2.2 Bonsai cultivar / FP8 substrate (ADR-2605092000–2605092300)\n\n| Workload | SSoT today | Cost-optimal alternative |\n|---|---|---|\n| Single-pod inference SSoT | RunPod 6000 Ada $0.74/hr (per-second) | unchanged — no provider beats this for prosumer Ada |\n| 24×7 H100 inference | n/a | **DO H100 Reserved $2.50/GPU/hr** (-9% vs Vultr BM, +K8s) |\n| Large-VRAM cohort fission (192–256 GB) | n/a | **DO MI300X Reserved $1.88/GPU/hr** ($10,979/mo per 8-pack, -49% vs Vultr) |\n| FP8 train+inference colocation (CDNA4) | n/a | **Vultr MI355X bare-metal $2.59/GPU/hr** if MI355X PyTorch ROCm path holds |\n| Burst Hopper (per-second) | RunPod H100 PCIe $2.39 | unchanged |\n\n### 2.3 Hypothesis disconfirmation\n\nUser hypothesis (2026-05-11 session): \"Vultr と RunPod は A40/A16 で価格差なく、L40S だけ大きく違う\"\n\nDisconfirmed:\n- A40: Vultr $1.71 vs RunPod $0.44 → **3.92× ratio (largest gap)**\n- L40S: Vultr $1.54 vs RunPod $0.79 → 1.95× ratio\n- A16: Vultr only ($1.88), RunPod未提供 → ratio undefined\n- H100 SXM: Vultr $2.75 vs RunPod $2.99 → **0.92× (Vultr cheaper)**\n\nThe actual pattern is \"RunPod beats Vultr on prosumer Ada; Vultr/DO win on enterprise Hopper/CDNA via committed pricing\".\n\n## 3. Action items (not blocking this ADR)\n\n| # | Item | Owner | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | Retry RW v2 schema (provider vertex + offers edge) and v3 INSERTs (DO 8× + reserved + MI350X/B300) | infra | RW barrier latency clears (compute-1 over-limit reconcile complete) |\n| 3.2 | Reconcile `helm/values.yaml` compute limit (24Gi live) ↔ `scaling-contract.yaml` recovery profile (15Gi) ↔ `deps.toml` (12Gi) | infra | before any RW topology change |\n| 3.3 | Decide on Bonsai cohort training provider (DO MI300X reserved vs Vultr MI355X) | research | when cohort fission rollout date set |\n| 3.4 | Resolve Vultr UKO-46CXG (cloud GPU plans for VKE node pools) | infra | external (Vultr support) |\n| 3.5 | Reconcile `graphar.*` aspirational naming with actual `public.*` placement OR migrate research tables to a `graphar` schema | research | sometime |\n| 3.6a | Apply Alembic revision `r_20260511022700_research_gpu_adr` (base tables: vertex_research_gpu_{model,plan,provider} + edge_research_plan_uses_gpu + edge_research_provider_offers_plan + vertex_research_adr + edge_research_adr_relates + 6 IDX). Path: `30-graph/graph-schema/alembic/current_versions/r_20260511022700_research_gpu_adr.py`. Apply via `DATABASE_URL=... pnpm db:migrate` from `30-graph/graph-schema/`. | infra | RW write path recovers (compute-1 over-limit reconcile) |\n| 3.6b | Apply SQLMesh models `mv_research_gpu_price_compare` + `mv_research_adr_graph` (`30-graph/graph-schema/sqlmesh/models/`) via `pnpm sqlmesh:plan` / `pnpm sqlmesh:run`. The current live `mv_research_gpu_price_compare` was created out-of-band by `_working/keiei/gpu-price-research-2026-05-11.sql` and must be reconciled (drop, let SQLMesh recreate). | infra | after 3.6a |\n| 3.6c | Run `_working/keiei/gpu-price-research-2026-05-11.sql` (v1) + `gpu-price-research-2026-05-11-v2.sql` + `gpu-price-research-2026-05-11-v3-data-only.sql` + `adr-ingest-2026-05-11.sql` as INSERT-only seed data. v1 is partially live already (32 plans / 15 models persisted); v2/v3 sneak-dropped under barrier latency. Adapt to record-log semantics (no ON CONFLICT). | infra | after 3.6b |\n| 3.6d | `DATABASE_URL=... pnpm db:gen` to regenerate `30-graph/graph-schema/src/database.ts` Kysely Row types for new tables. Then drop the `as any` casts in `50-infra/cloudflare/workers/atproto/src/mcp-adapter.ts handleResearch*` handlers. `pnpm db:drift` should pass after. | infra | after 3.6a (table existence) |\n| 3.7 | Run kotodama MCP bundle/deploy recipe for the new research tools added in `src/mcp-adapter.ts` (`etzhayyim.research.gpuPriceCompare`, `etzhayyim.research.listAdrs`) and lexicon JSON under `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/research/`: (1) `node 50-infra/cloudflare/workers/atproto/scripts/bundle-lexicons.mjs` (2) `node 70-tools/scripts/contract/gen-pds-lexicon-registry.mjs` (3) `cd 50-infra/cloudflare/workers/atproto && npx wrangler deploy` — per CLAUDE.md §LLM Coding Guardrails | infra | after 3.6b (MVs must exist) and 3.6d (types regenerated) |\n| 3.8 | After 3.7, exercise tools end-to-end: `etzhayyim mcp list-tools` then `tools/call etzhayyim.research.gpuPriceCompare {\"vramMinGb\":192}` and `tools/call etzhayyim.research.listAdrs {\"q\":\"kotoba\",\"authoritativeOnly\":true}` | research | after 3.7 |\n| 3.9a | sqlc adopted as query-layer codegen (multi-language type safety). Config at `30-graph/graph-schema/sqlc/sqlc.yaml`, queries under `query/`, generated TS under `gen/ts/` (gitignored). Run `pnpm sqlc:gen` after schema or query changes. Plugin: `sqlc-gen-typescript_0.1.3.wasm` (sha256-pinned). Compiled clean 2026-05-11 against schema/research.sql mirror. | research | done (this ADR) |\n| 3.9b | Add `pnpm db:gen --sqlc-schema` (or equivalent) to regenerate `30-graph/graph-schema/sqlc/schema/research.sql` from live RW `information_schema` so the sqlc DDL mirror cannot drift from the canonical schema (which is the live DB per ADR-2605080700). Until that exists, the mirror file is hand-maintained. | infra | followup |\n| 3.9c | Replace inline `sql.unsafe(...)` calls in mcp-adapter.ts research handlers with the sqlc-generated query string + arg interfaces. Runtime call shape: take generated `gpuPriceCompareListQuery` text, bind through Kysely's `sql<Row>\\`${rawQuery}\\``.execute(db)` or Hyperdrive's `.unsafe()`. This lifts the `as any` casts. | infra | after 3.6d |\n| 3.9d | Add the `sqlc-gen-python` plugin block + a second `codegen:` entry in `sqlc.yaml` once the first Python consumer needs typed access (likely SQLMesh DQ checks or a research CLI). Until then TS-only. | research | when first Python consumer arrives |\n\n## 5. MCP surface (ADR-0087 / ADR-2605091400 compliance)\n\nThis ADR also lands the first kotodama MCP facade tools that read RW research datasets directly:\n\n| Tool name | Lexicon | Backing relation | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `etzhayyim.research.gpuPriceCompare` | `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/research/gpuPriceCompare.json` | `public.mv_research_gpu_price_compare` | Live (after 3.7 deploy). |\n| `etzhayyim.research.listAdrs` | `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/research/listAdrs.json` | `public.mv_research_adr_graph` | Live after 3.6 (ingest) + 3.7 (deploy). |\n\nBoth handlers are inline in `50-infra/cloudflare/workers/atproto/src/mcp-adapter.ts` (`handleResearchGpuPriceCompare`, `handleResearchListAdrs`) following the `etzhayyim.schema` / `etzhayyim.vault.*` / `etzhayyim.context.*` inline pattern. They use `createKyselyDb(env.HYPERDRIVE)` and never expose secrets. No new account-level Worker required (research is read-only on the canonical RW MVs; routing-table dispatch unnecessary).\n\nLocal-skill alternative (psql shellout from `~/.claude/skills/`) was explicitly rejected by the operating principal per ADR-2605091400 (MCP = sole external API).\n\n## 4. Sources\n\n- Vultr API: `https://api.vultr.com/v2/plans?type=vcg` (cloud GPU) and `https://api.vultr.com/v2/plans-metal` (bare-metal)\n- DigitalOcean: `https://www.digitalocean.com/pricing/gpu-droplets`\n- RunPod Secure: `https://www.runpod.io/pricing` (per-second), cross-confirmed via `https://getdeploying.com/gpus/nvidia-l40s` and `https://getdeploying.com/gpus/nvidia-rtx-6000-ada`\n- Bandwidth Alliance (Backblaze B2 zero-egress members): `https://www.vultr.com/cloudalliance/backblaze/`, `https://www.backblaze.com/blog/backblaze-and-cloudflare-partner-to-provide-free-data-transfer/`\n- RunPod K8s incompat: `https://www.answeroverflow.com/m/1194359421904625746` + `https://github.com/BSVogler/k8s-runpod-kubelet` (community virtual-kubelet only)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605110227-gpu-cross-provider-pricing-research.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "gpu-pricing-cross-provider", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-11", :adr/date "2026-05-11", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605110100-vultr-a40-third-2node-consolidation" "adr-2605010000" "adr-2605092000-ecosystem-as-model-unified-multimodal-fp8-vector-substrate" "adr-2605092200-continuous-metabolic-training" "adr-2605092300-fp8-train-inference-colocation" "adr-0094-kotoba-stable-three-node-topology" "adr-0048-kotoba-vultr-b2-primary"], :adr/authoritative_for ["cross-provider $/GPU/hr table for NVIDIA A16/A40/L40/L40S/RTX-Ada/A100/H100/H200/B200/B300/GH200 + AMD MI300X/MI325X/MI350X/MI355X" "Bandwidth-Alliance + K8s-native eligibility per provider" "RunPod K8s incompatibility (Slurm-only Instant Cluster)" "DigitalOcean GPU Droplet full SKU lineup (1× / 8× / 12-mo reserved)"]}]
